&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Waymo’s Product Management Team is a mission-driven team responsible for writing and enacting first-of-their-kind playbooks to bring fully autonomous driving technology to market. Our team develops simple solutions for complex problems by orchestrating cross-functional efforts to safely drive Waymo’s technology and the products it enables forward. We do this by understanding the customer, the business, and the technology. We are humble about the scope of our work, collaborative in our approach to problem-solving, and ambitious about our vision for the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role follows a hybrid work schedule and reports to the Manager of Technical Program Management, Cybersecurity.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive the multi-year product security roadmap for the Waymo Driver and the vehicle platforms it integrates with, spanning embedded compute, sensors, vehicle networks, and the cloud services that provision, update, and operate our fleet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional security programs through hardware, embedded software, cloud infrastructure, manufacturing, and fleet operations teams, turning security goals into committed plans, owners, and milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive security requirements from threat analysis through implementation and verification, and own release security reporting: requirement coverage, open risks, exceptions, and readiness for each software and hardware release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frame trade-offs between security, performance, schedule, and operability as clear options, and drive decisions to completion with accountable owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive security across the full device lifecycle, from secure manufacturing and key provisioning through secure boot, over-the-air updates, field operations, and vulnerability response, until controls are verified across the deployed fleet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with vehicle and hardware platform partners, and keep programs aligned with applicable product security standards and regulations (e.g., ISO/SAE 21434, UN R155/R156) as Waymo expands internationally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant experience, including 5+ years of technical program management delivering hardware, embedded, or device-to-cloud products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on security background (e.g., security engineering, embedded or firmware security, product security architecture). You can explain how security controls work, how they fail, and what they cost to build, and you act as a technical peer to security and systems engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering security capabilities on shipped hardware or embedded products, such as secure or verified boot, hardware roots of trust (HSM, TPM, secure element, TEE), PKI and key management, code signing, secure OTA updates, or authenticated communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of delivering cross-functional programs through teams you did not manage, including getting security work prioritized against competing product goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience framing technical risk for decision makers and driving decisions through to execution, with clear communication to both engineers and executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A BS in Computer Science, Electrical or Computer Engineering, Cybersecurity, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior engineering experience in security, firmware, or embedded systems before moving into technical program management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing production fleets of connected devices (vehicles, robots, drones, consumer or industrial devices), including vulnerability response and verifying remediation across the deployed fleet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with secure manufacturing at contract manufacturers: device identity, key injection, and factory signing infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with real-time or in-vehicle networks and their security (e.g., CAN/CAN FD, Automotive Ethernet, SecOC, diagnostic authentication), or with safety-critical systems (e.g., ISO 26262, DO-178C, IEC 61508).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with product security standards and regulation (e.g., ISO/SAE 21434, UN R155/R156, IEC 62443, EU Cyber Resilience Act, FIPS 140-3) and threat analysis methods (TARA, STRIDE); experience building release security metrics and exception and risk-acceptance processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel requirements&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approximately 10%: quarterly team alignment in the Bay Area (for hires based outside the Bay Area), plus program travel to vehicle platform partners, manufacturing sites, and depots as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$196,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$242,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;FEQ427R441&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sr. Solutions Architect&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sr. Solutions Architect, you are an expert-level technical leader responsible for the organization&#39;s most complex customer engagements. You drive consumption strategy, own executive-level relationships, and serve as the definitive technical authority for your accounts. You have declared your archetype—a recognized technical specialization that makes you a force multiplier across your team and region. You operate at the intersection of deep technical expertise, strategic account planning, and executive influence.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Impact You Will Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the technical and consumption strategy for the organization&#39;s most complex customer engagements, directly influencing platform adoption and revenue growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own senior-level technical relationships — serving as a trusted advisor on enterprise data and AI strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the most complex architecture engagements: multi-workload platforms, enterprise-wide migrations, real-time systems, and AI/ML at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate as an Expert on the Databricks Platform with a declared archetype — actively mentoring others and driving horizontal impact across your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute competitive strategies for your customers, positioning Databricks against incumbent and emerging platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate cross-functional teams (DSAs, SSAs, Partners, Product) to deliver enterprise-grade solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop junior SAs (L3–L5) on technical depth, customer engagement, and use case prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Field Engineering thought leadership through customer-facing content, workshops, and community engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in solutions architecture, principal engineering, technical pre-sales leadership, or a senior customer-facing technical role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level coding proficiency — Python, SQL, and ideally Spark/PySpark. You will complete a live coding assessment and a platform build during the interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in enterprise data architecture: distributed systems at scale, streaming/real-time, lakehouse design patterns, data governance frameworks, and cloud-native platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level Databricks Platform knowledge (or equivalent depth in competing platforms with demonstrated rapid learning ability)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Declared technical specialization with recognized depth — e.g., real-time architectures, ML/AI platforms, data governance, large-scale migrations, or industry-specific solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of driving consumption growth and platform adoption in large accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence — ability to influence Directors, VPs, and C-level stakeholders on long-term data and AI strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading competitive displacements and complex enterprise evaluations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic thinking — connecting technical architecture decisions to business outcomes and revenue impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a quantitative discipline (or equivalent experience); advanced degrees are valued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Databricks certifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at Databricks, Snowflake, AWS, Google, Microsoft, or a top-tier data/AI company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Published thought leadership (blogs, conference talks, open source contributions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry vertical expertise with executive-level domain credibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview Process:&lt;/strong&gt; Recruiter Screen → Hiring Manager Screen → Design and Architecture Interview → Live Coding Assessment → Build, Demo, Pitch! Presentation → Reference Check&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Range Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Databricks is committed to fair and equitable compensation practices. The pay range(s) for this role is listed below and represents the expected base salary range for non-commissionable roles or on-target earnings for commissionable roles.&amp;nbsp; Actual compensation packages are based on several factors that are unique to each candidate, including but not limited to job-related skills, depth of experience, relevant certifications and training, and specific work location. Based on the factors above, Databricks anticipated utilizing the full width of the range. The total compensation package for this position may also include eligibility for annual performance bonus, equity, and the benefits listed above. For more information regarding which range your location is in visit our page &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.databricks.com/sites/default/files/2024-08/us-pay-zone-mapping.pdf&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$219,100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$301,300 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$219,100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$301,300 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$219,100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$301,300 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 4 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$219,100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$301,300 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
